From: DjDeveloperr <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:59:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] tmpfiles: keep the setup user's files non-executable

The recursive Z line set every file under /run/plasma-setup to 0750, so
the autostart entry copied there became executable and
systemd-xdg-autostart-generator warned on every login of the setup user:

  Configuration file /run/plasma-setup/.config/autostart/plasma-setup.desktop
  is marked executable. Please remove executable permission bits.

Mask the existing modes with ~0750 instead: directories still end up
0750, files keep their own non-executable mode.
---
 files/plasma-setup-tmpfiles.conf.in | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/files/plasma-setup-tmpfiles.conf.in b/files/plasma-setup-tmpfiles.conf.in
index 8ea1989..daf57ae 100644
--- a/files/plasma-setup-tmpfiles.conf.in
+++ b/files/plasma-setup-tmpfiles.conf.in
@@ -40,5 +40,7 @@ f /run/plasma-setup/.config/plasma-org.kde.plasma.desktop-appletsrc - - - - [Con
 # Install the customized global shortcuts config
 C+ /run/plasma-setup/.config/kglobalaccelrc - - - - ${CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_DATADIR}/plasma-setup/kglobalaccelrc
 
-# Recursively set the ownership of the home directory
-Z /run/plasma-setup 0750 plasma-setup plasma-setup - -
+# Recursively set the ownership of the home directory. The "~" masks each
+# file's own mode, so files keep it without gaining execute bits:
+# systemd-xdg-autostart-generator warns about an executable .desktop file.
+Z /run/plasma-setup ~0750 plasma-setup plasma-setup - -
